Article 2 (Duties of the Inspection and Audit Committee)
(1) The Inspection and Audit Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") shall discuss the following matters, and its chairperson shall present opinions based on the outcome of such discussions to the Minister of Justice and may recommend necessary measures: <Amended on December 31, 2008>
1. Matters concerning basic policies for operating the Office of the Inspector General;
2. Matters concerning basic annual plans for inspection and audit activities;
3. Matters concerning investigation methods and results and subsequent measures for major inspection and audit cases;
4. Other matters on which the Minister of Justice requests advice concerning inspections and audits.
(2) The term "major inspection and audit case" in paragraph (1) 3 means a case falling under any of the following: <Amended on June 12, 2006; April 28, 2020>
1. An inspection or audit case concerning a prosecutor, the head of an affiliated institution, the head of a subordinate organization, or a public official of Grade V or higher belonging to the Ministry of Justice or a prosecutors' office (including a public official belonging to the Senior Executive Service);
2. Any other inspection or audit case concerning a public official belonging to the Ministry of Justice or a prosecutors' office that the Minister of Justice or the Committee designates as an important case.
